# vergeio_member (Resource)

Add users or objects to groups in VergeIO. This resource manages group membership by associating a member (user or object) with a group. Changing `group` or `member` replaces the membership, because VergeOS does not allow a membership to be updated in place.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/vergeio_member/resource.tf" }}

Add a VM to a group.

{{ tffile "examples/resources/vergeio_member/resource_vm.tf" }}

<!-- schema generated by tfplugindocs -->
## Schema

### Required

- `group` (Number) - Key (ID) of the group to add the member to. Changing group replaces the membership.
- `member` (String) - Object to add in format `object_type/object_id` (e.g., `users/123`, `vms/456`). Changing member replaces the membership.

### Read-Only

- `id` (String) - Member ID in VergeIO

## Import

Import is supported using the resource ID:

```shell
terraform import vergeio_member.example <member_id>
```
